# Test appending to the description

This test verifies that `pebbles update --append-description` appends a line to
the description (newline-joined), stores the text verbatim when there is no
description, leaves the issue untouched when appending the empty string, and
combines with `--description` (replacement first, then append).

Fixture store: 12345678 (Test Issue, one-line description), 22222222 (Second
Issue, no description). Both are todo bugs.

## Show the initial description

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles show 12345678
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: 12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012
Title: Test Issue
Type: Bug
Status: TODO
Description: A test issue for trycmd validation

Created: [..]
Updated: [..]
File: bug-12345678-test-issue.json
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

```

## Append a line to the description

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles update 12345678 --append-description "Second line"
✓ Updated issue
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
