## Appending the empty string is a no-op

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles update 12345678 --append-description ""
No changes: nothing to update

```

## Replace then append in one update

Note: trycmd normalizes a backslash to a forward slash when comparing
fixture file contents, so the `Replaced/nTail` string in the `.out`
snapshot stands for the written JSON `Replaced\nTail` (one newline).

```console
$ PEBBLES_DB_PATH=.pebbles pebbles update 12345678 --description "Replaced" --append-description "Tail"
✓ Updated issue
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
ID: 12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012
Title: Test Issue
Type: Bug
Status: TODO
Description: Replaced
Tail

